                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:53.45pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>(</span> <span style='color:black'>xiv</span> <span style='color:black'>)</span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        If an industry has
                        obtained a valid rent permission from the authority to run its business,
                        applications of such applicants shall be considered under reserved/expansion
                        category. Incase the land is not allotted under reserved/expansion category,
                        such application shall be considered again under General category of plot
                        allotment. Conditions from (xiii) to(xiv) shall apply to applicants who have
                        obtained rent permission from NOIDA.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:6.0pt'>
                    <span style='color:black'>
                        4.3 <b>For industries applying under start up category</b>
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:64.35pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>(xv)</span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        Applications
                        for <b>start up firms</b> shall be considered separately. The other
                        eligibility conditions for such firms shall be under the guidelines issued
                        for Start-up firms from the Government time to time. Applicants under this
                        category shall furnish a certificate regarding their consideration under
                        startup based on their industry norms. Applicants should apply for only those
                        projects which are covered under Industrial Policy &amp; Procedure Oct 2012
                        as per Annexure III. Additionally please refer to point 6 while submitting
                        project report.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:64.35pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>(xvi)</span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        5 plots in
                        plot area 450 sq.mtr. category and 5 plots in &nbsp;plot area 1000 sq.mtr.
                        category have been reserved for startup firms.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:64.35pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>(xvii)</span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        Amongst these
                        plots, a draw shall be made to allot plot against the applications received
                        under this category.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:64.35pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>(xviii</span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        ) If the
                        applications received are less than the plots available, then plots left
                        after the draw shall be made available under open ended scheme for start up
                        firms.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:64.35pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>(xix)</span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        If the
                        applications received are greater than the plots available, then unsuccessful
                        applicants after the manual draw will be considered again under General
                        category of plot allotment, provided they meet the e ligibility for general
                        category plots.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:64.35pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt'>
                    <span style='color:black'>
                        Conditions from(xv) to (xix) shall apply to applicants
                        applying under start up firms category.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:53.45pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in'>
